course: dictionary
lesson: 11366
title: Words for people in charge
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An abbot is the man in charge of an abbey. An abbey is a community of monks who live, pray and work together. «The abbot rang the bell to call the monks to prayers.» Here the abbot is the leader who tells everyone when to pray.
explain: Think of the abbot as the head of a very special school for monks. He keeps the abbey's rules, looks after its lands and money, and makes sure everyone has what they need. «The abbot kept the rules of the abbey and checked the harvest.»
explain: In history, an abbot could be even more powerful than a leader of a monastery. In the Middle Ages he could own land and be as important as a lord. «The abbot owned fields and villages, just like the lord of the castle.» Context helps you see that abbot can mean a powerful landowner, not only a monk's leader.
explain: Use the swap trick to check. Put «the man in charge of an abbey» in place of abbot. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. A woman who leads a community of nuns is called an abbess, so the two words are a pair.
fact: An abbot is the man in charge of an abbey.
fact: An abbey is a community of monks who live, pray and work together.
fact: In the Middle Ages, an abbot could also be a powerful landowner, as important as a lord.
fact: A woman who leads a community of nuns is called an abbess.
fact: In stories, an abbot is often wise, but sometimes he can be greedy or strict.
exercise: «The abbot rang the bell to call the monks to prayer.» Who is the abbot? | A woman who leads the nuns | *A man in charge of an abbey | A king who lives in a castle | A young boy who sings in the choir
exercise: What is an abbey? | A tall tower in a castle | *A community of monks who live, pray and work together | A school for young children | A shop that sells bread
exercise: «The abbot kept the monks busy and looked after the abbey's lands.» Find and copy the word for the men who live and pray together in an abbey. | *monks | lands | looked | busy
test: In the Middle Ages, an abbot could own land and be as important as a lord. What does this tell you about an abbot then? | He had no land or money at all | *He could be a powerful landowner | He was a farmer who sold eggs at the market | He was a servant who only cooked
test: The abbot is a man. What is the word for a woman who leads a community of nuns? | Monk | Abbot | Lord | *Abbess
exam: «In the story, the wise abbot gave the lord some good advice.» What is the abbot like in this story? | Greedy and rude | *Wise, and he gives good advice | A young child who cannot read | Lazy and silly
